      label((4.6, 6.0), [the wizard: only inside], col: glow, size: 13pt)
    })),
    [
      The scene mixes millimetre fingers with a 150-unit horizon. One march over everything would take tiny steps all the way.

      #v(0.3em)
      So each ray is marched twice: through the *land* along its whole length, and through the *wizard, rock and glows* only inside a sphere around him. The nearer hit wins.

      #v(0.3em)
      #note[Every part also has a *layer* bit, so one scene function serves the camera, the shadows (only some parts cast them) and debugging toggles.]
